    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/36B3F450786FDD30DEED3E70ECBB75B9/jobs/457033": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant - OPG/LAW",
      "description": "You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Administrative Assistant - OPG/LAW MIAMI GARDENS, FL 33054 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Apply St. Thomas University - Office of Public Guardian POSITION SUMMARY: This is a grant-funded position that assists in carrying out administrative functions through facilitating the accomplishment of the work of the Office of the Public Guardian by assisting with legal, clerical, and informational services, and integrating them with the administration of the office served. Position schedule is Monday through Friday from 9 AM to 5 PM. Office is located in Davie, Florida. CHARACTERISTIC DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES: Serves as the administrative assistant to the Office of the Public Guardian. Composes correspondence and memos from verbal instruction or notes, answers mail requiring critical thinking skills to plan, organize, and set up in proper form. Input’s client data in the client database system. Conducts initial phone screening to assess eligibility of potential new clients. Schedules meetings, takes meeting minutes, and arranges appointments. Maintains a system of interrelated files and records. Prepares and monitors regular or special reports on departmental activities and modifies or devises forms for reporting data and establishes controls for accuracy of data. Answers telephone, takes messages, and replies to questions in accordance with general instructions. Transmits instructions and/or information to and from staff members and assists with document filing functions. Maintains and updates an office manual, setting forth the necessary elements of procedure, required forms and steps necessary to carry out the job functions necessary for the efficient operation of the Office of the Public Guardian. Collaborates with guardian representatives, benefits and eligibility coordinator, fiscal specialist, and paralegal in all aspects of ward entitlement applications and maintenance including applications for ICP, Social Security and SSI benefits. Collaborates with guardian representatives, benefits and eligibility coordinator, fiscal specialist, and paralegal in monitoring and tracking DCF interviews and redeterminations as needed and all ward related matters. Collects and maintains data for statistical reports for the public guardian office and the wards served. Monitors ward reports and court filing due dates and prepares tracking instruments for task status. Assists the legal team with preparing legal documents, e-filing, and related functions. Regularly reviews, classifies, and distributes incoming mail including confidential correspondence. Regularly assesses the program needs such as office supplies and assures that supplies are ordered timely. Performs other related duties as assigned by Executive Director. Qualifications POSITION QUALIFICATIONS/SPECIFICATIONS: High School diploma or GED required. Associate degree, or vocational, or technical school degree in Business Administration or related field required. Minimum of 3-5 years’ work experience. Working knowledge of concepts, practices and procedures and ability to use in varied situations. Detail-oriented with the ability to multitask. Assumes responsibility readily, seeking out issues and areas needing resolution and development. Knowledge of Word, Excel, Outlook, SharePoint, Guardianship Data Base Is able to work with a minimum of supervision exercising judgment to make decisions. Able to draft correspondence/memos, revise legal templates, and interpret guardianship statutes. Knowledge of Florida Guardianship Statute 744. Possesses a high level of integrity and inter personal skill necessary for dealing with all levels of the public, Probate Judges, court personnel, representatives from SSA, VA, DCF, Financial Institutions, family member/friends of wards, and facilities where OPG wards reside. Is able to work with a minimum of supervision exercising judgment to make decisions. Must pass a level II background check and a credit check reviewed and monitored by the Statewide Public Guardianship Office and by the 17th Judicial Circuit. Must complete and successfully pass the 40-Hour Guardianship Class within one year of employment. Must successfully pass the Florida State Guardianship Exam within one year of employment Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/36B3F450786FDD30DEED3E70ECBB75B9/jobs/474886": {
      "title": "Associate Dean of Nursing",
      "description": "You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Associate Dean of Nursing MIAMI GARDENS, FL 33054 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Apply St. Thomas University - College of Nursing Position Summary The Associate Dean of Nursing at St. Thomas University is an on-campus leadership position based at the Miami Gardens, FL campus; this is not a remote or online role, and the incumbent is expected to maintain a consistent physical presence on campus. The Associate Dean serves as an essential member of the College of Nursing’s leadership team. As the operational academic leader of the College, the Associate Dean partners with the Dean to translate strategic priorities into coordinated action aligning people, processes, and resources to support high-quality program delivery. The incumbent supports curricular innovation, accreditation efforts, faculty mentorship, and student success, ensuring students are thoroughly prepared for professional success within the nursing field. Location: St. Thomas University – Miami Gardens, FL (On-Campus; Not a Remote or Online Position) Key Responsibilities: Strategic Leadership: Collaborate with the Dean and academic leadership to articulate, refine, and implement the vision, mission, and strategic goals of the College of Nursing. Ensure that all programs including BSN, RN–BSN, ABSN, MSN, DNP, and certificate offerings reflect the highest standards of academic quality and integrity. Curriculum Oversight: Collaborate with the Dean, Program Directors, and the curriculum leadership team to support the development, implementation, and continuous improvement of curriculum. Ensure alignment with accreditation standards (CCNE, SACSCOC, and state Board of Nursing) and national frameworks, including competency-based education (CBE) and the AACN Essentials. The Associate Dean facilitates implementation and coordination of curriculum processes but does not independently determine program-level curricular decisions. Faculty Development: Provide supervision, mentorship, and professional growth opportunities for faculty. Oversee recruitment, onboarding, and comprehensive evaluation of faculty performance, fostering an inclusive and supportive academic environment. Clinical and Experiential Education: Lead the coordination of clinical placements and the advancement of simulation-based learning, cultivating strong partnerships with healthcare organizations to enrich students’ experiential learning opportunities. Student Success Initiatives: Monitor student performance indicators, including retention, graduation rates, and NCLEX/Certification pass rates. Design and implement targeted interventions to enhance student achievement and support academic progression. Accreditation and Quality Assurance: Direct ongoing efforts to maintain accreditation, ensuring continuous compliance with all relevant regulatory bodies, and preparing thorough documentation and reports as required. The Associate Dean supports accreditation activities; however, primary accountability for accreditation oversight remains with the Dean. Academic Operations: Oversee academic scheduling, faculty workload distribution, and resource allocation to ensure optimal program delivery and operational efficiency. Community and Stakeholder Engagement: Represent the College at institutional and external events, and cultivate effective relationships with alumni, clinical partners, and the broader nursing community. Teach up to 3-4 undergraduate/graduate nursing courses annually. Operational Leadership & Implementation Lead the coordination and execution of academic operations across all nursing programs. Oversee implementation of institutional and college-level initiatives. Ensure alignment between curriculum, faculty processes, and operational systems. Monitor execution of academic policies, procedures, and timelines. Coordinate cross-functional initiatives involving faculty, Program Directors, and administrative staff. Collaboration with Program Leadership Support Program Directors in the execution of program operations and academic initiatives. Facilitate communication and coordination across programs. Convene regular Program Director meetings to ensure alignment and operational effectiveness. Maintain a collaborative, service-oriented leadership approach that supports (but does not replace) Program Directors authority. Faculty Operations & Support Oversee faculty onboarding, orientation, and ongoing support. Coordinate faculty development initiatives aligned with curriculum and instructional needs. Assist in the faculty evaluation process, including drafting annual evaluations for review by the Dean. Support adjunct faculty processes in collaboration with the Director of Online Nursing Operations. Coordination with Director of Online Nursing Operations Collaborate closely with the Director of Online Nursing Operations to ensure effective delivery of online programs. Support alignment between faculty onboarding, course delivery, and academic expectations. Coordinate operational processes related to adjunct faculty, course readiness, and scheduling. Ensure consistency and quality across online course offerings in partnership with program leadership. Project & Initiative Leadership Lead and/or support implementation teams for strategic academic initiatives. Work collaboratively with faculty subject matter experts in areas such as competency-based education, curriculum design, and assessment. Ensure initiatives are implemented using a collaborative, team-based model that promotes shared expertise and faculty engagement. Qualifications Qualifications Earned doctoral degree in Nursing or a closely related discipline (DNP, PhD, or equivalent) required. Current unencumbered Registered Nurse license in the State of Florida, or eligibility for licensure. Advanced Practice Registered Nurse (APRN) certification or licensure preferred. Substantial experience in academic leadership, program development, and faculty oversight within an accredited nursing program. Comprehensive knowledge of accreditation standards and regulatory requirements (CCNE, CNEA, SACSCOC, state Board of Nursing). Demonstrated commitment to fostering student achievement and supporting a diverse learning environment. Exceptional leadership, communication, and organizational skills. Compensation & Benefits Salary range: commensurate with experience, qualifications, and aligns with regional standards. Full benefits including health, dental, vision, disability insurance, retirement plan, paid holidays, and flexible time off. Application Process Candidates should submit: Cover letter addressing leadership, curriculum, and student success experience. Current CV. Contact information for three professional references. Official transcripts (for final candidates; foreign degrees require credential evaluation). Review of applications begins immediately and continues until the position is filled. About St. Thomas University – College of Nursing Located in Miami Gardens, STU’s College of Nursing offers a comprehensive range of nursing programs (BSN, RN–BSN, MSN, DNP, and specialty certificates) with a strong emphasis on community health, clinical excellence, and experiential learning. The College is accredited by CCNE and affiliated with local healthcare systems to support robust clinical and simulation-based training environments. Working at STU means contributing to a culturally diverse, inclusive educational environment that prepares nursing professionals to serve Florida’s communities with excellence. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/36B3F450786FDD30DEED3E70ECBB75B9/jobs/440361": {
      "title": "Associate Law Library Director",
      "description": "You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Associate Law Library Director MIAMI GARDENS, FL 33054 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Apply St. Thomas University - College of Law Summary Under the direction of the Law Library Director, this staff member will be primarily responsible to oversee the overall functioning of the Law Library with direct supervision over the heads of all Law Library functions and staff. They will assist the Law Library Director on all administrative library workflow matters and responsible for the administration of the Law Library in the Director’s absence. Essential Functions Associate Librarian Duties In collaboration with the Law Library Director, provide strategic guidance on how the law library can be most effective in teaching, research, and providing services to the College of Law, the University, and other constituents. Assist in developing the law library’s mission, vision, and values, to support the College of Law’s mission and strategic plan as well as the University’s mission and strategic plan. Assist with the development of all law library policies. Assist the Director in library administration and coordination of interdepartmental activities withinthe library. Supervise the law library in the director’s absence. Implement and oversee the law library’s human resources policies, including recruitment, hiring, evaluation and training. Oversee and coordinate Law Library staff vacation requests and absence reports. Direct the hiring of student assistants Interview and participate in the selection of assigned staff; conduct performance appraisals and suggest professional development opportunities in accordance with university policies and procedures. Assist the Director by in coordinating all facilities management services and issues dealing with the Office of Physical Plantand all telecommunications needs with the Law School Administration. Coordinate Law Library membership in the different cooperating consortia, professional organizations, or any other groups to which the Law Library belongs to. Maintain and provide information an d s t at is t ic s an d assist with preparing reports for ABA, SEFLIN, SACS, Department of Education, and other accrediting agencies. Monitor the expenses of the faculty book account in consultation with the Faculty Services and Scholarly Communications Librarian and communicate with the faculty when necessary. Recommend the organizational structure, staffing and functional responsibilities of the law library. Assist the director in communications with library vendors and Collection Management Services to ensure proper resources are made available. Assist the Director with strategic planning and long-term initiatives with the Law Library and University Library system. Assist the Director in oversight of the STU Audiovisual department with regard to law school classroom technologies and support. Public Services Duties Provide research and reference support to all library patrons. Lead the development and maintenance of research guides, bibliographic tools, the law library webpage Coordinate and teach guest lectures, lunch and learns, and other curricular and extra-curricular programming that involves general and specialized legal research. Prepare instructional material and training sessions and participate in legal research instructional programs as requested or needed by law school faculty or student organizations. Assist with collection development with emphasis on non-print material. Keep statistics on special project and assignments. In the absence of the Faculty Services Librarian, provide direct support to the Law School faculty for research, materials, and training requests including Canvas, Westlaw/TWEN, LexisNexis/Lexis Classroom, Bloomberg Law and other law school technologies and resources. Participates in general Reference & Research services as part of regular workflow, including regular shifts at the reference desk. Other duties Represent the Law Library in local, regional, and national meetings as requested. Serve on University and/or Law School Committees and participate in University and Law School events as requested. Keep informed of new trends in access services and the law profession. Recommend materials and services to Library Administration based upon current trends in use amongst faculty and students. Teach courses in legal research and legal writing as needed in coordination with the Associate Dean for Academic Affairs and the Director of Legal Writing. Competencies Strong and effective communication skills, both oral and written. Strong supervisory skills with the ability to manage and develop staff. Strong interpersonal skills including the ability to work effectively with students and faculty from a wide diversity of background and educational experiences. Organizational, planning, and administrative skills including the ability to work effectively on broad as well as detailed projects. Ability to work in a network environment including working with an integrated library system. Knowledge and ability to work with legal databases and common law school and educational technologies, and the ability to design library instructional tools. Strong technical skills, interest in technology, and the ability to troubleshoot simple technology problems, failures, or deficiencies- expertise with law school technologies such as TWEN, Lexis Classroom, Canvas, is essential. Ability to understand library system technology that can be used to improve services, instruction efforts and workflows. Strong service orientation and effective problem-solving skills. Be flexible with work assignments and work hours. Supervisory Responsibility This position has direct supervision of law librarians and heads of Law Library sub-units. This position indirectly supervises any staff, including work-study students, engaged by these departments. Work Environment/Physical Demands The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. While performing the duties of this job, the employee is occasionally required to stand, walk; sit; reach with hands and arms; climb stairs; push library carts full of books; climb on stands to shelf books. The employee must occasionally lift or move library materials and supplies, up to 30 pounds. Position Type/Expected Hours of Work This is a full-time position. Days and hours of work are Monday through Friday, 10 a.m. to 6 p.m. This position occasionally requires schedule changes with weekend/evening hours. Travel Travel is primarily for Professional Development. The employee will be asked to represent the Law Library in local, regional, and national meetings as requested by the Library Director. Qualifications Education and Experience M.L.S. from an A.L.A. accredited library school program is required. J.D. from an accredited ABA institution is required. Previous academic law library experience is required. Three or more years of experience in law libraries is preferred. One or more years of supervisory experience is required. Previous library administration experience strongly preferred. Other Duties Please note this job description is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time with or without notice. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/36B3F450786FDD30DEED3E70ECBB75B9/jobs/463903": {
      "title": "Campus Plumber/Plumbing Specialist",
      "description": "You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Campus Plumber/Plumbing Specialist MIAMI GARDENS, FL 33054 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Apply St. Thomas University - Physical Plant Position Summary Under the general supervision of Facilities Operations leadership, the Campus Plumber performs skilled and semi-skilled plumbing maintenance, repair, installation, and preventive maintenance across the university campus. This includes academic buildings, residence halls, athletic facilities, and administrative spaces. The position ensures the safe, efficient, and continuous operation of all water distribution, drainage, backflow, and plumbing fixture systems across campus. Essential Duties & Responsibilities Routine & Emergency Maintenance: Inspect, troubleshoot, and repair domestic hot/cold water supply systems, drainage, sanitary sewer lines, storm drains, and vent piping. Respond promptly to urgent leaks, line blockages, and plumbing emergencies campus-wide. Fixture Repair & Replacement: Repair or replace toilets, urinals, flush valves (manual and sensor-operated), faucets, sinks, showers, drinking fountains, water heaters, and garbage disposals. Preventative Maintenance: Perform scheduled preventative maintenance on campus pumps (circulator, sump, lift station), valves, backflow preventers, and piping assemblies. Maintain routine logs and digital work order records within the campus maintenance management system (CMMS). System Inspections & Troubleshooting: Clear drain blockages using motorized drain augers, hydro-jetters, and specialized diagnostic equipment. Read and interpret building blueprints, mechanical schematics, and system layouts. Modifications & Upgrades: Measure, cut, thread, solder, crimp, and assemble piping (copper, PVC, CPVC, PEX, cast iron) for minor capital improvements or facility modifications. Safety & Code Compliance: Ensure all work adheres to Miami-Dade County plumbing codes, OSHA standards, and university safety protocols. Maintain safe work areas and proper PPE during hazardous or elevated work. Vendor & Project Coordination: Assist facilities leadership in scope verification and inspection for third-party plumbing contractors working on major campus renovation or construction projects. General Department Support: Support overall Physical Plant operations during major campus events, emergency weather prep (e.g., hurricane prep/post-storm recovery), and other duties as assigned by leadership Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: Education: High School Diploma or GED equivalent. Vocational or technical school training in plumbing preferred. Experience: Minimum 3–5 years of commercial or institutional plumbing maintenance experience. Higher education campus experience is a plus. Licensure / Certifications: Valid State of Florida Driver’s License (Required). Miami-Dade County Journeyman/Master Plumber License or equivalent trade certification (Preferred/Required depending on level). Backflow Prevention Certification (ASSE 5110 or equivalent) (Preferred). Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Thorough knowledge of commercial plumbing equipment, tools, fittings, materials, and local plumbing code requirements. Ability to utilize electronic work order tracking software (CMMS) on desktop/mobile devices. Strong problem-solving abilities with high attention to work safety and cleanliness. Good interpersonal and communication skills to work effectively with students, faculty, staff, and external vendors in a university setting. Physical Demands & Working Conditions Must be able to lift, push, pull, or carry up to 50–70 lbs regularly. Requires climbing ladders, crouching, crawling in tight spaces, standing for extended periods, and working both indoors and outdoors in South Florida weather conditions. Occasional exposure to grease, dirt, wastewater, chemicals, high temperatures, and loud environments. Must be available for rotation on-call duties or emergency response outside standard working hours. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/36B3F450786FDD30DEED3E70ECBB75B9/jobs/455041": {
      "title": "Director of Student Engagement and Events",
      "description": "You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Director of Student Engagement and Events MIAMI GARDENS, FL 33054 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Apply St. Thomas University - Student Life POSITION SUMMARY : The Director of Student Engagement and Events provide strategic leadership for the University’s comprehensive student engagement program by developing meaningful co-curricular experiences that foster student success, leadership development, school spirit, campus traditions, and a strong sense of belonging. The Director oversees campus programming, major institutional events, student organizations, Student Government Association (SGA), the Campus Activities Board (CAB), leadership initiatives, and student involvement efforts. This position is responsible for creating innovative programming that enhances the student experience while supporting recruitment, retention, persistence, and graduation. The Director collaborates with academic and administrative departments to create a vibrant campus culture that promotes holistic student development. CHARACTERISTIC DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Leadership & Strategic Planning Provide strategic leadership and vision for all student engagement initiatives. Develop and implement a comprehensive campus engagement strategy aligned with the University’s strategic plan. Establish measurable goals, learning outcomes, and assessment plans for student engagement. Serve as a member of the Student Life leadership team. Prepare annual reports, assessment data, and strategic recommendations for senior leadership. Campus Programming & Events Plan, coordinate, and evaluate a comprehensive calendar of campus events throughout the academic year. Lead the planning and execution of major institutional programs including: Week of Welcome New Student Orientation Homecoming Leadership Retreats Cultural Heritage Month Program Late-Night Programmin Student Appreciation Events Commencement-related student activities Oversee event logistics including contracts, vendors, risk management, budgeting, reservations, and event staffing. Ensure all events promote student engagement, inclusion, and campus traditions. Student Organizations Oversee the recognition, development, and support of all registered student organizations. Advise student leaders regarding organizational management, budgeting, event planning, and leadership development. Develop policies and procedures governing student organizations. Facilitate annual student organization registration and officer transitions. Promote student organization recruitment and involvement opportunities. Student Government Association (SGA) Serve as the primary advisor to the Student Government Association. Guide student leaders in governance, leadership, budgeting, advocacy, and programming. Assist with elections, officer transitions, constitutional compliance, and leadership training. Support SGA initiatives that enhance the student experience and campus community. Campus Activities Board (CAB) Provide direct oversight and advise the Campus Activities Board. Support student leaders in planning engaging social, educational, cultural, and entertainment programming. Assist in developing innovative programming responsive to student interests. Ensure responsible stewardship of CAB budgets and resources. Leadership Development Develop leadership education initiatives for students. Coordinate leadership conferences, retreats, workshops, and training programs. Create opportunities for emerging and experienced student leaders to develop professional competencies. Promote civic engagement, service learning, and community involvement. Student Involvement Develop strategies to increase student participation and campus involvement. Utilize engagement assessment tools to identify student interests and participation trends. Coordinate involvement fairs and student organization recruitment events. Promote engagement opportunities through effective communication and marketing. Budget & Fiscal Management Develop and manage departmental operating budgets. Oversee funding allocations for student organizations, CAB, and SGA. Monitor expenditures and ensure responsible fiscal management. Approve contracts, purchase requests, and vendor payments. Qualifications POSITION QUALIFICATIONS/SPECIFICATIONS: Minimum Qualifications Master’s degree in Higher Education, Student Affairs, College Student Personnel, Educational Leadership, Counseling, or a closely related field. Minimum of 2 years of progressively responsible professional experience in university housing or residential life. Minimum of 1 year of supervisory experience. Experience managing budgets and housing occupancy. Demonstrated experience in crisis management and student conduct. Excellent written, verbal, organizational, and interpersonal communication skills. Ability to work evenings, weekends, holidays, and participate in an emergency on-call rotation. Preferred Qualifications Experience supervising multiple residence halls housing over 1,000 students. Experience with housing management software such as StarRez. Experience with assessment, accreditation, and strategic planning. Knowledge of living-learning communities and residential curriculum models. Experience in facilities planning and capital improvement projects. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Strong leadership and team development skills. Excellent conflict resolution and crisis management abilities. Knowledge of student development theory and higher education best practices. Ability to analyze data and make informed decisions. Exceptional customer service and relationship-building skills. Ability to manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment. Strong presentation and public speaking skills. Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite and student information systems. Physical Requirements Ability to move throughout campus and residence halls. Ability to lift up to 25 pounds occasionally. Ability to respond to emergencies during evenings and weekends. Work Environment The Director works in a dynamic higher education environment requiring frequent interaction with students, faculty, staff, parents, and external partners. The position requires flexibility to respond to emergencies and participate in evening and weekend activities as needed. Supervisory Responsibilities The Director directly supervises: Associate Director(s) (if applicable) Student Engagement Coordinators Campus Activities Board Advisor/Coordinator Graduate Assistants Student Office Assistants Federal Work Studies Student Event Staff Indirect supervision includes: Student Government Association Executive Board Campus Activities Board Executive Board Student Organization Leaders COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS: Full-Time | Exempt Administrative | Staff Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/36B3F450786FDD30DEED3E70ECBB75B9/jobs/470282": {
      "title": "Eligibility and Benefits Coordinator",
      "description": "You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Eligibility and Benefits Coordinator Davie , FL 33330 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Apply St. Thomas University - Office of Public Guardian POSITION SUMMARY : The Benefits and Eligibility Coordinator is responsible for coordinating, obtaining, maintaining, and monitoring governmental benefits and entitlements programs on behalf of the clients served by the Office of the Public Guardian. The Benefits and Eligibility Coordinator serves as a liaison between the Public Guardian Program and federal, state, county, and local agencies, including, but not limited to, the Social Security Administration (SSA), Florida Department of Children and Families (DCF), U.S. Department of Veterans Affairs (VA), Medicaid Long-Term Care programs, and the Area Agency on Aging of Broward County. This position is responsible for identifying benefits for which Wards may be eligible; completing and submitting applications, renewals, redetermination, and other required documentation; monitoring eligibility requirements and deadlines; and taking appropriate action to obtain new benefits and prevent the unnecessary interruption or loss of existing benefits. The Benefits and Eligibility Coordinator works closely with Guardian Representatives, facilities, physicians, case managers, healthcare providers, financial staff, and other appropriate parties to obtain the information and documentation necessary to establish and maintain each Ward’s benefits and entitlements. The position requires regular follow-up with government agencies and other entities and may require travel to local agencies, facilities, or other locations as necessary to complete benefit-related matters on behalf of Wards. CHARACTERISTIC DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : The Benefits and Eligibility Coordinator will: Research available federal, state, county, and local benefit and entitlements programs and identify programs for which Wards served may qualify. Complete, submit, monitor, and track applications for new benefits, renewals, recertifications, and annual redeterminations within all required deadlines. Maintain an organized and reliable tracking system for all benefit applications, renewals, redeterminations, requests for information, appointments, deadlines, pending matters, and required follow-up. Proactively monitor benefit expiration and renewal dates and initiate the necessary action sufficiently in advance to prevent avoidable delays, interruptions, or termination of benefits. Obtain and review information and documentation necessary to complete benefit applications and maintain eligibility, including financial, medical, residential, and other supporting documentation. Notify appropriate agencies of changes affecting a Ward’s eligibility or benefits, including changes in residence, income, assets, medical status, level of care, or other relevant circumstances. Communicate and coordinate with physicians, healthcare providers, facilities, Guardian Representatives, case managers, financial personnel, and other appropriate parties to obtain documentation required by federal, state, county, and local agencies. Notify appropriate agencies and provide required documentation when a Ward has been appointed a legal guardian, when there is a change in guardianship status, or upon the death of a Ward. Investigate, troubleshoot, and assist in resolving issues involving delayed, denied, suspended, reduced, or terminated benefits. Respond timely to agency requests for additional information, verification, documentation, interviews, or other actions necessary to establish or maintain benefits. Maintain regular communication with the appropriate Guardian Representative and other program staff regarding the status of applications, pending matters, outstanding documentation, approaching deadlines, and issues requiring attention. Document benefit-related activity, correspondence, applications, approvals, denials, notices, and follow-up in the Ward’s electronic record and/or paper file in accordance with program procedures. Ensure that entitlement and benefits information in each Ward’s record is accurate, complete, and current. Maintain reports and tracking tools that clearly identify the status of each Ward’s benefits, pending applications, renewal dates, outstanding items, deadlines, and follow-up actions. Maintain copies of applications, confirmations, correspondence, notices, eligibility determinations, and other supporting documentation in the appropriate Ward record. Schedule and maintain appointments with government agencies and other entities as necessary and ensure required appointments, interviews, and deadlines are met. Follow up consistently on pending applications and unresolved benefit matters until a determination or resolution is received and documented. Remain knowledgeable regarding changes to federal, state, and local benefit programs, eligibility requirements, application procedures, and reporting requirements, and communicate relevant changes to appropriate program staff. Protect the confidentiality of Ward information and comply with applicable program policies and legal requirements concerning confidential and sensitive information. Travel to government offices, facilities, healthcare providers, and other locations as necessary to complete benefit-related responsibilities. Perform additional duties and responsibilities as assigned by the Executive Director and/or Associate Director. Qualifications POSITION QUALIFICATIONS/SPECIFICATIONS : Bachelor’s degree (B.A. or B.S.) in Business, Finance, or Social Work from an accredited college/university. Minimum of two (2) years of professional experience working with public benefits, government entitlement programs, eligibility determination, social services, guardianship, case management, or a related field. Knowledge of, or demonstrated ability to learn, public benefit programs including Social Security, Supplemental Security Income (SSI), Medicaid, Medicare, Medicaid Long-Term Care, Veterans benefits, and other federal, state, and local assistance programs applicable to the population served. Proficiency with Microsoft Office applications, including Word, Excel, and Outlook, as well as internet-based systems, electronic records, databases, and other internal and external software applications. Strong organizational and time-management skills with the ability to manage multiple cases, applications, deadlines, and follow-up requirements simultaneously. Demonstrated initiative and ability to work independently, prioritize responsibilities, identify problems, and follow matters through to resolution. Strong problem-solving, research, documentation, and follow-up skills Effective written and verbal communication skills and the ability to communicate professionally with government agencies, healthcare providers, facilities, program staff, Wards, and other involved parties. Ability to maintain accurate and detailed records and handle confidential information appropriately. Must successfully complete all required background screening, including a Level II background screening, and any other screening required by the program or applicable law. Must possess a valid driver’s license and have reliable transportation to travel to agencies, facilities, and other locations as required by the position. Must successfully complete the required 40-Hour Guardianship Training Course within one (1) year of employment. Must successfully pass the Florida guardianship competency examination within one (1) year of employment, if required for the position. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/36B3F450786FDD30DEED3E70ECBB75B9/jobs/409826": {
      "title": "Financial Specialist",
      "description": "You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Financial Specialist MIAMI GARDENS, FL 33054 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Category Education Apply St. Thomas University - Office of Public Guardian Position Summary: This position performs a variety of accounting and bookkeeping functions in support of the Office of the Public Guardian (OPG). Expert knowledge of QuickBooks and Excel, along with experience in the accounting or finance field, is required, or an equivalent combination of education, proven expertise, and experience in bookkeeping, accounting, or financial management with a strong understanding of accounting principles and practices and knowledge of Social Security benefits and eligibility. This position is subject to review by Court Administration, the Social Security Administration, and the Florida State Auditor. The role is responsible for the management and marshalling of all fiscal client needs, including income tax preparation, court accountings, asset inventories, and required financial reports. Additionally, this position must be able to perform audits and ensure ongoing compliance with established auditing standards and internal protocols. Essential Functions: Prepares timely and accurate net asset values, yields, distributions, and other fund accounting output on OPG client accounts for subsequent review. Documents and recommends client financial transactions and actions by entering account information and analyzing accounting options. Summarizes current client financial status by collecting information, preparing balance sheets, profit and loss statements, and other required reports. Substantiates financial transactions by auditing client documents. Prepares payments by verifying documentation and requesting/issuing disbursements via the clients’ independent bank account. Maintains financial security by following internal controls and protects operations by keeping financial information confidential. Answering accounting procedure questions by researching and interpreting accounting policy and regulations. Prepares special financial reports by collecting, analyzing, and summarizing account information and trends. Complies with federal, state, and local, financial legal requirements by studying existing and new legislation and enforcing adherence to requirements as related to guardianship asset management and other programmatic needs. Prepares the yearly income tax form for the OPG clients (when applicable). OPG Program and Grants Assists the Program’s Executive Director in overseeing and monitoring compliance with State contractual requirements and State regulations, procedures, and policies. Consistently reviews accounting related policies to ensure compliance with University and State regulations. Budgets, monitors, maintains, and supervises monthly income and expenditures records for Public Guardian (OPG) clients/wards and compiles periodic reports, including annual accounting reports to the Probate Court and the Social Security Administration. Issues payments, research expenditures, solves problems, and authorizes bank transactions with Executive Director/Public Guardian approval. Reconciles bank statements with ward accounts and monthly bank deposits. Maintains wards’ records by routing all fiscal documents accordingly and by supervising ward account balances. Analyzes revenue and expenditure trends and recommends appropriate budget levels to ensure expenditure control of wards. Communicate detailed information via various types of secure communication formats to representatives of the department of Children and Families, Social Security, Veterans’ Administration, as well as authorizes and consents to entitlement related functions. Collaborates with guardian representatives in all aspects of ward entitlement applications and maintenance including applications for Medicaid, Social Security and SSI benefits. Collaborates with program Benefits and Eligibility Coordinator and monitors and tracks telephone DCF interviews and redetermination requirements as needed and collaborates with guardian representatives in this area. Collects and maintains data for statistical reports for the programs and wards and prepares tracking instruments for task status. Collaborates with the grants department and provides bank reconciliation reports in a timely manner. Maintains a system of interrelated files and records. Prepares regular or special reports on department fiscal activities and modifies or devises forms for reporting data and establishes controls for accuracy of data. Monitors and issues monthly SSA Organizational Representative Payee check vouchers. Transmits instructions and/or sensitive information to and from staff members. Answers incoming calls, takes messages, and responds to inquiries in accordance with general office procedures and instructions. Reviews, classifies, and distributes incoming mail including confidential correspondence. Performs other related duties incidental to the work described herein as assigned by the program executive director. Will complete the 40-Hour Guardianship and successfully pass the state Guardianship exam within one year of employment. Qualifications Candidates must have a solid understanding of accounting principles and practices, including financial recordkeeping, reconciliation, reporting, and financial management procedures. Knowledge of Social Security benefits, eligibility requirements, and related regulations is also required. An equivalent combination of education, specialized training, proven expertise, and relevant professional experience in bookkeeping, accounting, or financial management may be considered in lieu of a formal degree. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/36B3F450786FDD30DEED3E70ECBB75B9/jobs/470220": {
      "title": "Floor Technician",
      "description": "You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Floor Technician MIAMI GARDENS, FL 33054 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Apply St. Thomas University - Physical Plant Summary The Floor Care Technician performs assigned floor care functions based on St. Thomas University standards and procedures. In addition to this, the floor technician performs environmental services as needed and strips, waxes, and buffs floor on an as needed basis. Essential Functions Cleaning offices, hallways, and common areas Cleaning, dusting, mopping, stripping and waxing floors Measuring chemicals appropriately Operating floor equipment that includes but not limited to T5 auto-scrubber, ride along auto- scrubber, burnishes, and carpet extractors Keeping inventory of floor equipment and recording the hours used each day Breaking down floor equipment Assisting with hazardous waste collection Competencies Team Oriented Great Communicator Results Driven Responsible Supervisory Responsibility N/A Work Environment/Physical Demands The work environment is professional. Physically fellow employee must be able to lift/push/pull/carry up to or more than 70 pounds. May be required to work evenings and irregular hours to complete floor projects Position Type/Expected Hours of Work Custodial Position/Expected hours per week will be 37.5 hours. This is subject to change based on the needs of the University Travel This position does not require any traveling off campus. Qualifications Required Education and Experience High School Diploma or GED equivalent Preferred Education and Experience 5+ years’ of Floor Care experience Must be able to lift/push/pull/carry up to or more than 70 pounds Good knowledge of custodial services, practices and procedures Additional Eligibility Qualifications N/A Other Duties Please note this job description is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities and activities may change at any time with or without notice. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/36B3F450786FDD30DEED3E70ECBB75B9/jobs/473318": {
      "title": "Full-time Faculty: Supply Chain/Trade and Logistics Management",
      "description": "You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Full-time Faculty: Supply Chain/Trade and Logistics Management MIAMI GARDENS, FL 33054 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Apply St. Thomas University - Gus Machado College of Business Full-time Faculty: Supply Chain/Trade and Logistics Management Gus Machado College of Business | St. Thomas University | Miami Gardens, Florida St. Thomas University (STU) invites applications for a full-time faculty member for the Enrique V. Del Riego Institute of Trade & Logistics, under the Gus Machado College of Business. The ideal candidate will be an innovative, industry-engaged, and student-centered faculty with expertise in Supply Chain Management, Logistics Management, International Trade, and related areas. The successful candidate will provide academic and strategic support for the Institute while teaching, mentoring students, providing academic advising, advancing applied research, strengthening industry partnerships, and assisting with the implementation and stewardship of grants and donor-supported initiatives. The position offers an opportunity to help shape the continued development of a multidisciplinary academic and workforce platform connecting business education, supply chain, logistics, international trade, accounting, finance, technology, research, and industry engagement. The Opportunity This position provides the opportunity to contribute to the continued development and growth of the Enrique V. Del Riego Institute of Trade and Logistics Institute as a distinctive academic, workforce-development, research, and industry-engaged unit of the Gus Machado College of Business at St. Thomas University. This full-time faculty will be expected to connect academic excellence with hands-on learning and industry practice, creating meaningful opportunities for students while strengthening the Institute's and College’s relationships with employers, government agencies, professional organizations, donors, and community partners. Essential Responsibilities Provide academic instruction for courses in Supply Chain, Logistics Management, International Business and other related areas within the College of Business, through lectures, hands-on learning, applied exercises, projects, simulations, and other experiential approaches. These expectations build directly on STU's existing faculty model for this academic area. Mentor undergraduate and graduate students and supervise research, capstone, and applied projects. Maintain on-ground faculty office hours and attend department, college and university meetings and events as required. Maintain scholarly, applied research, professional, and service activities appropriate to the faculty appointment. Assist curriculum development, program enhancement, and continuous improvement of academic, certificate, micro credentials, and workforce offerings. Strengthen interdisciplinary connections among Supply Chain, Logistics Management, International Trade, Business, Accounting, Finance, technology, and related disciplines. Build and sustain relationships with employers, logistics and transportation organizations, ports, airports, import/export organizations, government agencies, professional associations, and other industry partners. Expand internships, apprenticeships, experiential learning, applied research, professional certifications, and employment pathways for students. Assist with the preparation and contribute to grant reports, donor stewardship reports, impact reports, presentations, and other documentation demonstrating measurable results. Identify opportunities for external funding, industry partnerships, applied research, workforce initiatives, and program growth. Represent the Institute and St. Thomas University with industry, academic, governmental, donor, and community stakeholders. Foster interdisciplinary collaborations and partnerships to showcase the Enrique V. Del Riego Institute of Trade and Logistics Management. Academic Focus Candidates with expertise or professional experience in one or more of the following areas are particularly encouraged: Supply Chain Management Logistics Management International Trade Supply Chain Analytics Logistics and Operations Management Green and Sustainable Supply Chains Transportation and Distribution Aviation Logistics Maritime Logistics Ground Transportation Global Supply Chains Procurement and Inventory Management Import/Export Operations Customs and Trade Compliance International Finance and Trade Finance Digital Supply Chains Artificial Intelligence and Automation in Logistics Supply Chain Risk and Resilience Qualifications Qualifications Preferred Qualifications: Doctoral degree from a regionally accredited institution in Supply Chain Management, Logistics Management, Business Administration, International Business, Operations Management, or related field. Minimum Qualifications: Master's degree from a regionally accredited institution in Supply Chain Management, Logistics Management, International Trade, Business Administration, Operations Management, Information Systems/Technology, Accounting, Finance, or a closely related field. Demonstrated professional and/or academic expertise in Supply Chain Management, Logistics Management, International Trade, or related disciplines. Proven ability to teach college-level courses effectively. Demonstrated commitment to student-centered, hands-on, and experiential learning. Evidence of or potential for scholarly, applied, or professional work in relevant disciplines. Demonstrated industry experience. Experience in curriculum development, academic programming, workforce development, or related educational initiatives. Strong leadership, communication, organizational, and relationship-building skills. The Successful Candidate The successful candidate will have a passion for teaching, hands-on learning, research, student mentoring, and industry engagement and will be comfortable interacting in the classroom, and with academic and university leadership and industry partners. The individual should possess the ability to engage with professionals throughout the Supply Chain, Logistics Management, and International Trade sectors and translate emerging industry needs into relevant educational, research, and workforce opportunities for students. About St. Thomas University St. Thomas University is a Catholic, student-centered university located in Miami Gardens, Florida, dedicated to developing ethical leaders for life. The University offers undergraduate, graduate, law, and doctoral education and is committed to academic excellence, professional preparation, scholarship, service, and student success. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
