    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/36B3F450786FDD30DEED3E70ECBB75B9/jobs/454752": {
      "title": "Groundskeeper",
      "description": "You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Groundskeeper MIAMI GARDENS, FL 33054 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Apply St. Thomas University - Physical Plant Job Summary: The Groundskeeper is responsible for maintaining the beauty, cleanliness, and safety of the university’s outdoor spaces, including lawns, walkways, gardens, courtyards, athletic areas, and landscaping surrounding campus buildings. This role helps support a welcoming environment that reflects the Catholic university’s mission, values, and commitment to stewardship of campus resources. Duties typically include mowing, trimming, planting, pruning, irrigation support, litter removal, and seasonal grounds care. Key Responsibilities : Maintain lawns, trees, shrubs, flower beds, and landscaped areas through mowing, edging, trimming, weeding, watering, mulching, fertilizing, and pruning. Collect and remove trash, leaves, branches, and other debris from campus grounds, sidewalks, parking areas, and outdoor gathering spaces. Operate and perform basic maintenance on grounds equipment and hand tools, such as mowers, trimmers, blowers, edgers, rakes, and irrigation tools. Assist with planting trees, flowers, shrubs, and seasonal displays, and help prepare soil and planting areas. Support irrigation system checks, basic repairs, and watering schedules as needed. Help prepare outdoor areas for university events, liturgies, ceremonies, and special campus activities. Perform seasonal duties such as leaf removal, storm cleanup, snow or ice response where applicable, and general campus beautification. Qualifications Qualifications : High school diploma or equivalent preferred. One year of groundskeeping, landscaping, or related maintenance experience preferred. Ability to safely operate grounds equipment and use hand tools. Basic knowledge of plant care, turf maintenance, and irrigation systems. Ability to work outdoors in varying weather conditions and perform physical labor, including lifting, bending, standing, and walking for extended periods. Working Conditions : This position requires frequent outdoor work in heat, humidity, rain, and other seasonal conditions. The Groundskeeper may be assigned early morning, evening, weekend, or event-related shifts depending on campus needs. The role involves exposure to equipment, noise, chemicals, dust, and physically demanding tasks. Application Process: To apply for the Groundskeeper position, please submit your resume and a cover letter detailing your relevant experience and why you are a perfect fit for the role. Company Values : At St. Thomas University, we are committed to creating a cleaner and safer environment for everyone. We value teamwork, integrity, and dedication in our pursuit of excellence. Join us to be part of a dynamic team striving for high-quality service delivery. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/36B3F450786FDD30DEED3E70ECBB75B9/jobs/403633": {
      "title": "Housekeeper",
      "description": "You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Housekeeper MIAMI GARDENS, FL 33054 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Apply St. Thomas University - Physical Plant Position Summary: The Housekeeper is responsible for maintaining cleanliness, sanitation, and overall appearance of assigned areas on campus, including classrooms, offices, restrooms, hallways, and dormitories. This position helps ensure a clean and safe environment for students, staff, and visitors. Key Responsibilities: Sweep, mop, and vacuum floors Clean and sanitize restrooms, including sinks, toilets, mirrors, and floors Empty trash and recycling bins and replace liners Dust furniture, window sills, and other surfaces Restock restroom supplies (toilet paper, soap, paper towels) Clean windows, walls, and doors as needed Report any maintenance issues or safety hazards Follow all safety and cleaning protocols Assist with event setup and cleanup when required Qualifications Qualifications: High school diploma or equivalent preferred Previous housekeeping or janitorial experience is a plus Ability to lift up to 40 lbs and stand for long periods Must be reliable, punctual, and able to work independently or as part of a team Must be able to follow written and verbal instructions Work Schedule: Flexible shifts available. May include evenings or weekends based on campus needs. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
