      "description": "You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Maintenance Technician - South Hall MIAMI GARDENS, FL 33054 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Apply St. Thomas University - Physical Plant POSITION SUMMARY Under the general supervision of the Manager, Facilities Operations, performs building repairs, preventative maintenance, and minor carpentry work dedicated to South Hall and its surrounding immediate premises. CHARACTERISTIC DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Perform minor repairs and/or replacement of plumbing fixtures, valves, and other devices within South Hall restrooms, common areas, and facilities. Perform minor repairs and/or replacement of electrical fixtures, devices, and appliances throughout South Hall as required. Perform minor carpentry work as required to repair windows, doors, and furniture in South Hall rooms, offices, and hallways. Prepare materials lists for work orders and estimate time required for jobs in South Hall. Hang sheetrock/wallboard and apply tape and spackling compound to achieve a finished paintable surface. Hang doors and maintain door hardware, locks, and entryways in South Hall. Replace damaged ceiling tiles and floor tiles throughout South Hall. Perform concrete and masonry repairs on South Hall walkways, entrances, and exterior structures. Assist in the moving of furniture and with event set-ups within South Hall. Serve on University committees as requested. Perform other duties as assigned by the immediate supervisor. SUPERVISION RECEIVED Routine assignments are performed independently following University and departmental policies and procedures. SUPERVISION EXERCISED Works independently using own judgment. Qualifications POSITION QUALIFICATIONS / SPECIFICATIONS Able to communicate both orally and in writing. Valid Florida Driver's License. Three years of experience in the building maintenance field. Must be familiar with general building maintenance trades. Ability to operate power saws, drills, grinders, sanders, and other power hand tools connected with the maintenance and carpentry trade. Ability to work 1st shift hours as assigned. May be required to lift, push, or pull up to 70 lbs. May be exposed to chemicals, mechanical, or electrical hazards. May be exposed to dust, fumes, or odoriferous working conditions. May be required to work outdoors in inclement weather. Employee is required to wear protective clothing or devices. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
