    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/36B3F450786FDD30DEED3E70ECBB75B9/jobs/408072": {
      "title": "Public Safety Dispatcher",
      "description": "You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Public Safety Dispatcher MIAMI GARDENS, FL 33054 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Category Education Apply St. Thomas University - Public Safety POSITION SUMMARY: The University Public Safety Communications Dispatcher serves as the central communications link for campus public safety and police operations. The dispatcher is responsible for receiving emergency and non-emergency calls for service, dispatching university public safety personnel, monitoring security systems, and maintaining situational awareness across campus. The incumbent is part of the Fusion Center network, coordinating the exchange of threat intelligence, suspicious activity reporting, and public safety information. This position plays a critical role in coordinating emergency response, documenting incidents, and supporting crime reporting and safety operations to protect the university community. Emergency Communications Receive and process emergency and non-emergency calls for service from the campus community. Determine priority of calls and dispatch appropriate public safety, police, fire, or medical response. Provide emergency call assistance and instructions when necessary. Maintain constant communication with officers and responders during incidents. Dispatch Operations Dispatch university public safety personnel using radio and computer-aided dispatch (CAD) systems. Monitor officer status, assignments, and locations. Coordinate responses with external law enforcement, fire rescue, and emergency management agencies when required. Security Systems Monitoring: Monitor CCTV camera systems, intrusion alarms, fire alarms, access control systems, and emergency call boxes. Identify suspicious or criminal activity and notify responding personnel. Maintain awareness of campus safety conditions and incidents in progress. Incident Documentation and Reporting: Maintain accurate call logs and incident records in CAD or records management systems. Document calls for service, officer activities, and response actions. Prepare Public Safety and Police Reports as warranted. Ensure records support compliance reporting including crime statistics under the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act. Emergency Notification and Campus Alerts: Assist with activation of campus emergency notification systems when directed. Notify Public Safety Leadership and other stakeholders as directed, regarding incidents on campus. Support communication efforts during emergencies, severe weather, or critical incidents. Serve as scribe, dispatcher, or ICS role during the activation of the Incident Command Post. Operational Intelligence and Situational Awareness: Monitor communications and security technologies to maintain campus situational awareness. Identify potential incident trends or unusual activity and notify supervisors. Provide real-time information to responding officers and command staff. Customer Service: Provide professional assistance and information to students, faculty, staff, and visitors in person and by telephone. Assist with parking citations, parking decals, and other administrative duties as directed by superior. Maintain calm and effective communication during high-stress situations. Qualifications MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS High school diploma or equivalent required. Prior experience in public safety dispatch, law enforcement communications, or emergency call center preferred. Ability to work rotating shifts including nights, weekends, and holidays, as well as serve as essential personnel during critical incidents, weather events, special events and operations. Strong multitasking and decision-making skills in fast-paced environments. Preferred Experience with Computer-Aided Dispatch (CAD) systems. Experience in campus public safety or law enforcement communications. Certification in emergency telecommunications or public safety dispatch. Knowledge of federal campus safety reporting requirements. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/36B3F450786FDD30DEED3E70ECBB75B9/jobs/435439": {
      "title": "Public Safety Officer I",
      "description": "You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Public Safety Officer I MIAMI GARDENS, FL 33054 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Apply St. Thomas University - Public Safety POSITION SUMMARY: The non-exempt hourly position is a specialized public safety officer I (PSO) responsible for maintaining safety, security, and order within the University campus, residence halls, and surrounding footprint. They serve as a visible presence, support student wellbeing, and coordinate closely with university stakeholders including Office of Student Affairs and Student Life, Office of Residential Living, faculty, and staff. This is a 24-hour operation which requires the ability to work an atypical schedule to meet operational necessity, with varied shifts, including weekends and holidays. This position is classified as essential personnel and may require reporting to duty during emergencies or natural disasters, and special events. Adherence to established public safety uniform and grooming standards is mandatory. ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES: Patrol campus on golf cart, vehicle or on foot, inclusive of Residential Halls Respond to noise complaints or disturbances Monitor CCTV or alarm systems Escort students, faculty and staff upon request Conduct Safety checks (doors, lighting, emergency equipment) in collaboration with Resident Assistance Incident documentation and communication with dispatch Detect and respond to safety hazards to ensure safety of students, faculty, staff and visitors. Provide physical inspections and investigation on campus to ensure a safe environment. Conduct security and safety audits to ensure that hazards and dangers are identified. Conduct Residential Room checks in collaboration with the Office of Residential Life. Conducts accident and injury investigations on campus to ensure proper record keeping of incidents. Complete activity logs, inspection reports and incident reports to ensure proper record keeping of incidents. Coordinate with local University Leadership, Clery Administrators, local law enforcement concerning the investigation of incidents, crimes, and losses. Attend collaboration meetings with Office of Residential Life, Resident Assistants, and other University stakeholders. Conduct fire systems, life safety inspections and emergency response drills. Lock and unlock access control for campus buildings. Perform other duties as assigned or required. Qualifications MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: High School degree or equivalent. Valid driver's license. Not have been convicted of any felony or of a misdemeanor involving perjury or false statement. Any person who, after July 1, 1981, pleads guilty or nolo contendere to, or is found guilty of a felony or of a misdemeanor involving perjury or a false statement, shall not be eligible for employment or appointment as an officer notwithstanding suspension of sentence or withholding of adjudication Successfully pass a background investigation, that may include drug testing Good communication skills and the ability to interact effectively in a diversified community. Excellent customer service skills necessary. No Dishonorable Discharge from the Military Good communication skills and the ability to interact effectively in a diversified community. Excellent customer service skills necessary. Must be responsible, dependable and punctual. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS: Previous experience in customer service driven public safety field. Experience in University or school setting. Previous experience as a Resident Assistant. State of Florida Class D and/or G License. Previous Military or Law Enforcement. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/36B3F450786FDD30DEED3E70ECBB75B9/jobs/468975": {
      "title": "Public Safety Operations Manager (Interim)",
      "description": "You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Public Safety Operations Manager (Interim) MIAMI GARDENS, FL 33054 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Apply St. Thomas University - Public Safety POSITION SUMMARY: The Public Safety Operations Manager is responsible for assisting the AVP with residence hall security, CCTV and other technology monitoring and prevention systems for the university on a 24-hour, 365 days per year basis. They assist with managing various unpredictable caseload demands, with the ability to direct, coordinate, and review assignments and projects. The Public Safety Operations Manager assists with training, and supervising non-sworn Campus Safety officers; assists with planning and implementing security operations, programs, and initiatives in support of the University’s mission and vision. Additionally, the Public Safety Operations Manager, as the Incident Commander for crisis situations, is responsible for the conducting of exercises with the senior administration to test and refine emergency plans. The Public Safety Operations Manager is responsible for assisting in other areas such as: Departmental In-Service training, Parking and Traffic issues, and all security requirements for University sponsored events on campus. ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES: Assist with supervising, and training, and ensures the proper training levels and the certifications for staff are achieved. Assist with leading all efforts related to crisis management planning, operations, and campus activities in the event of an actual crisis. Assists with forming and maintaining strong and productive relationships with various external civil authorities, with special attention given to the Miami Gardens Police and Fire Department liaisons. Assist as Liaisons with Marketing and Communications staff in crisis situations relative to campus-wide alerts and messaging protocols. Assists with overseeing parking registration, enforcement, and appeals. Assists with evaluating performance of staff and administers discipline, if necessary. Assists with preparing and reporting crime statistics and ensures complete compliance with FERPA, HIPPA, and Clery. Assists in working with Residence Life Staff and Student Affairs in the enforcement and University policy. Assists in preparing reviews and distributes daily morning reports and incident reports. Assist with ensuring staff always maintains a professional appearance and demeanor within the Campus Safety department. Assists with meeting daily with University personnel to discuss all issues relative to the safety and security of the University community. Assists with serving in an on-call capacity to ensure emergencies are adequately addressed. Assists with conducting ongoing departmental assessments of services and programs. Assists with in completing monthly and annual reports for the department. Support and implement the divisional and University mission and strategic plan. Qualifications MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS High School diploma or GED Experience in an educational/campus safety setting strongly preferred. Demonstrate strong team leadership talents, managerial skills, and organizational skills. Strong writing skills. Demonstrated commitment to diversity. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/36B3F450786FDD30DEED3E70ECBB75B9/jobs/449431": {
      "title": "Resident Director II",
      "description": "You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Resident Director II MIAMI GARDENS, FL 33054 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Apply St. Thomas University - Residential Community Living POSITION SUMMARY : The Resident Director (RD) is a full-time, live-in professional staff member responsible for fostering a safe, inclusive, and supportive living-learning environment for residential students. This entry-level role is ideal for individuals interested in beginning a career in student affairs or higher education. The RD oversees the day-to-day management of a residential area, supervises student staff, and supports student development through programming, community building, and crisis response. CHARACTERISTIC DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Supervise, train, and evaluate a team of Resident Assistants (RAs) Foster a positive and inclusive residential community that promotes student engagement and academic success Plan and support educational and social programs aligned with departmental and institutional goals Serve as a conduct officer for policy violations within the assigned residential area Respond to emergencies and participate in an on-call duty rotation Maintain visibility and availability to students through regular office hours and community presence Collaborate with campus partners, including Public Safety, Counseling Services, and Academic Support Manage administrative responsibilities such as occupancy reports, room condition records, and incident documentation Assist with student check-in, check-out, and room selection processes Promote a safe and respectful living environment by enforcing community standards Other duties as assigned SUPERVISION RECEIVED : Incumbent works with university policies and general objectives, referring to supervisors for clarification and interpretation of broad university policies and procedures or programmatic references. Qualifications POSITION QUALIFICATIONS/SPECIFICATIONS: Bachelor’s degree required; Experience in Higher Education, Student Affairs, Counseling, or related field preferred. Experience in residence life or student leadership roles (e.g., RA, peer mentor, orientation leader) Strong interpersonal, communication, and organizational skills Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a diverse community Demonstrated commitment to student development and inclusive practices COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS: Competitive entry-level salary Fully furnished apartment Meal plan included during academic terms Professional development opportunities Health, dental, and vision insurance (if applicable) Tuition Benefit (based on institutional policy) Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
