    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/36B3F450786FDD30DEED3E70ECBB75B9/jobs/460384": {
      "title": "System Analyst",
      "description": "You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account System Analyst MIAMI GARDENS, FL 33054 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Category Information Technology Apply St. Thomas University - Office of Information Technology OVERVIEW Analyze data processing topics to develop and implement solutions to complex applications problems, system administration issues, or network concerns. Perform systems management and integration functions, improve existing computer systems, and review computer system capabilities, workflow, and schedule limitations. Analyze or recommend commercially available software. CHARACTERISTIC DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES: Determine computer software or hardware needed to set up or alter systems. Use object-oriented programming languages, as well as client and server applications development processes and multimedia and Internet technology. Test, maintain, and monitor computer programs and systems, including coordinating the installation of computer programs and systems. Troubleshoot program and system malfunctions to restore normal functioning. Provide staff and users with assistance solving computer-related problems, such as malfunctions and program problems. Coordinate and link the computer systems within an organization to increase compatibility so that information can be shared. Analyze information processing or computation needs and plan and design computer systems, using techniques such as structured analysis, data modeling, and information engineering. Consult with management to ensure agreement on system principles. Specify inputs accessed by the system and plan the distribution and use of the results. Expand or modify system to serve new purposes or improve work flow. Read manuals, periodicals, and technical reports to learn how to develop programs that meet staff and user requirements. Develop, document, and revise system design procedures, test procedures, and quality standards. Recommend new equipment or software packages. Define the goals of the system and devise flow charts and diagrams describing logical operational steps of programs. Review and analyze computer printouts and performance indicators to locate code problems, and correct errors by correcting codes. Supervise computer programmers or other systems analysts or serve as project leaders for particular systems projects. Qualifications POSITION QUALIFICATIONS/SPECIFICATIONS: Education and experience Junior Analyst: High school diploma Analyst: Associate’s Degree or 1 year experience as analyst Senior Analyst: Bachelor’s Degree or 3 years experience as analyst Principal Analyst: Master’s Degree or 7 years experience as analyst Significant experience with Microsoft Server software and SQL databases Significant experience with one or more applications used at St. Thomas University: Ellucian Colleague, Instructure Canvas, Slate CRM, Microsoft Office Suite, Cousedog, or Hyland Perceptive Content. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/36B3F450786FDD30DEED3E70ECBB75B9/jobs/470266": {
      "title": "Trash Technician",
      "description": "You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Trash Technician MIAMI GARDENS, FL 33054 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Apply St. Thomas University - Physical Plant Position Summary: The Trash Technician is responsible for making sure the campus grounds are free of debris and trash. In addition, the position is to maintain all the University's trash, recycling bins, designated compactor areas etc. Essential Functions: Collects and transports general waste, recycling, and soiled linens in accordance with department guidelines. Collects and transports recyclable materials. Operates power equipment in the completion of assignments, which include the trash compactor and forklift. May be called upon to perform conventional housekeeping-related duties in other areas as needed. Responsible for the arrangement and setup of meeting rooms, including the transport and stocking of supplies. Responds to customer Service requests. Must collaborate with others, organize well, accomplish tasks, solve problems, and communicate effectively. Competencies: STANDARDS OF BEHAVIOR : Acts in a manner that supports the standards of communication, respect, privacy, and teamwork by demonstrating a commitment to professional and ethical conduct. CUSTOMER SERVICE: Demonstrates commitment to service excellence by promptly addressing internal/external customer issues/requests, resolving concerns while maintaining a professional image and behavior to build and enhance the patient/family/customer experience. ACCOUNTABILITY: Accepts ownership of job roles and specific assignments/goals; works independently, takes responsibility for own actions; admits mistakes and judgment errors; and accepts constructive feedback. Connects personal work results to the accomplishment of team and organizational goals. RESPONDING TO CHANGE: Accepts change and adapts in a positive and productive manner; handles unexpected situations and changes in direction calmly and with confidence. View new assignments and job responsibilities as an opportunity for growth. ENVIRONMENTAL SERVICES: Maintains a clean and safe environment, enhancing the facility's appearance. ROOM CLEANING AND CHECKOUT: Utilizes appropriate guidelines for sanitizing and preparing patient rooms. FLOOR CARE: Provides a safe and sanitary environment by maintaining a consistent floor care program. Qualifications Required Education and Experience: High School diploma or GED preferred. Ability to read, write, speak English, including comprehension of verbal and written instructions, correspondence and memos is highly preferred. Must be able to prioritize job duties and be able to work independently and/or in a team environment. Prior experience in floor care maintenance is highly preferred. Additional Eligibility Qualifications: Required to stand, push, pull, reach, lift, bend, and walk for extended periods of time. Required to lift 50-75 pounds occasionally, and 25 pounds regularly. Must be able to push/pull carts weighing 50 pounds on a regular basis. Work Environment/Physical Demands: Required to stand, push, pull, reach, lift, bend, and walk for extended periods of time. Required to lift 50-75 pounds occasionally, and 25 pounds regularly. Position Type/Expected Hours of Work: This position is expected to work a minimum of 37.5 hours per week. This position will be working outdoors for most of the day. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/36B3F450786FDD30DEED3E70ECBB75B9/jobs/466076": {
      "title": "University Librarian",
      "description": "You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account University Librarian MIAMI GARDENS, FL 33054 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Apply St. Thomas University - University Library Summar y The Dean of STU Libraries provides strategic leadership and administrative oversight for the University's entire library ecosystem, including the University Library, Law Library, and Collection Management. This role is responsible for ensuring uniformity of service and equitable access to resources across all branches, serving as a bridge between academic goals and operational excellence. The University Librarian ensures that library services, digital resources, and physical facilities evolve consistently to meet the diverse needs of undergraduate and graduate students. A key collaborator across campus, they manage high-level personnel, maintain budgetary stability, and oversee complex accreditation compliance (SACS, ABA, IPEDS) to guarantee a high standard of academic support university-wide. The Dean of STU Libraries also serves as the University Library Director, the Law Library Director, or the Director for Collection Management Services, which will remain their primary function . Essential Functions Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Provide vision and leadership for the Library System in support of the University's mission and goals. Plan, develop, and deliver high quality library services that are accessible to all undergraduate and graduate students. Establish a process of ongoing review, assessment and improvement of library programs, resources and services that will evolve along with student needs and expectations. Collaborate with the directors of the university's academic and student support services to leverage strengths and expand opportunities to address student needs. Manage the library systems operations with a focus on ongoing improvements within a stable budgetary context. Develop, maintain, and review library system policies. Implement and oversee the library systems human resources policies, including recruitment, hiring, evaluation, and training. Interview and participate in the selection of assigned staff; conduct performance appraisals and suggest professional development opportunities in accordance with university policies and procedures. Supervise directly heads of library sub-units: University Library, Law Library, and Collection Management Services. Coordinate Library membership in different cooperating consortia, professional organizations, and any other organization the libraries may belong to. Maintain and provide information and statistics; assist with preparing reports for accrediting agencies and reporting agencies including, but not limited to: SACS, ABA, Department of Education, IPEDS, SEFLIN, and others. Coordinate with the head's of library sub-units to ensure that the libraries collections are sufficient to meet the needs of STU programs and students. Oversee building maintenance and cleaning services by interfacing directly with the Office of Physical Plant. Propose updating and maintenance as needed. Keep statistics on special project and assignments. Other duties Represent STU Libraries in local, regional, and national meetings as requested. Serve on University and/or Law School Committees and participate in University events as requested. Keep informed of new trends in library services and the legal profession. Com p etencies Strong and effective communication skills, both oral and written. Strong supervisory skills with the ability to manage and develop staff. Strong interpersonal skills including the ability to work effectively with students and faculty from a wide diversity of background and educational experiences. Organizational, planning, and administrative skills including the ability to work effectively on broad as well as detailed projects. Ability to work in a network environment including working with an integrated library system. Knowledge and ability to work with academic databases and common higher-education technologies and instruction tools. Knowledge and ability to work with legal databases and common law school and educational technologies, and the ability to design library instructional tools. Strong technical skills, interest in technology, and the ability to troubleshoot simple technology problems, failures, or deficiencies. Ability to understand library system technology that can be used to improve services, instruction efforts and workflows and assess effectiveness of technologies. Strong service orientation and effective problem-solving skills. Being flexible with work assignments and work hours. Commitment to higher education and STU's mission. Su p ervisor y Res p onsibilit y This position has direct supervision over heads of Library sub-units, including University Library, Law Library, and Collection Management Services. This position indirectly supervises any staff, including work-study students, engaged by these departments. Work Environment / Ph y sical Demands The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. While performing the duties of this job, the employee is occasionally required to stand, walk; sit; reach with hands and arms; climb stairs; push library carts full of books; climb on stands to shelf books. The employee must occasionally lift or move library materials and supplies, up to 30 pounds. Position T yp e / Ex p ected Hours of Work This is a full-time position. Days and hours of work may be flexible due to the nature of the position, but this individual is generally expected to be on campus Monday- Friday during business hours. This position occasionally requires schedule changes with weekend/evening hours. Travel Travel is primarily for Professional Development. The employee may represent the University at regional and national conferences at their discretion in coordination with the University Provost or the Dean of the College of Law. The Librarian may be asked to attend other regional and national conferences. Qualifications Re q uired Education and Ex p erience M.L.S. from an A.L.A. accredited library school program is required. Previous academic library experience is required. Three or more years of experience in law libraries is preferred. Three or more years of supervisory experience is required. Previous library administrative experience required. J.D. from an accredited ABA institution is required if the University Librarian also servers as Director of the Law Library . Other Duties Please note this job description is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities and activities may change at any time with or without notice. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/36B3F450786FDD30DEED3E70ECBB75B9/jobs/474306": {
      "title": "Visiting Instructor/Visiting Assistant Professor of Mathematics",
      "description": "You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Visiting Instructor/Visiting Assistant Professor of Mathematics MIAMI GARDENS, FL 33054 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Apply St. Thomas University - Health Sciences and Technology St. Thomas University in Miami Gardens, Florida, invites applications for a full-time visiting faculty position in Mathematics for Spring 2027. This is a one-semester appointment, with the possibility of consideration for a continuing full-time position beginning Fall 2027. We are seeking a dependable, student-focused faculty member who is comfortable teaching a range of undergraduate mathematics courses. The primary responsibility of this position is teaching and supporting student success. Responsibilities: Teach a full-time undergraduate mathematics course load. Teach courses that may include College Algebra, Precalculus, Calculus, and Statistics, depending on departmental needs. Maintain regular office hours and provide academic support to students. Work collaboratively with mathematics faculty on common course materials, assessments, and student success initiatives. Participate in departmental activities as needed. Qualifications Qualifications Master's degree or higher in Mathematics, Statistics, Applied Mathematics, or a closely related field, with at least 18 graduate credit hours in mathematics or statistics. Ability to teach undergraduate Statistics is required. Ability to teach College Algebra and other introductory mathematics courses. Strong communication and organizational skills. Commitment to teaching and supporting students with a wide range of mathematical preparation. College-level teaching experience is preferred. Experience with Canvas, ALEKS, or similar instructional technology is helpful but not required. Candidates with a Ph.D. may be considered at the Visiting Assistant Professor level. Catholic Identity St. Thomas University is a Catholic university sponsored by the Archdiocese of Miami. Employees are expected to respect and support the University's mission and values. Position Details Position: Full-time, Spring 2027 Location: St. Thomas University, Miami Gardens, Florida Work arrangement: In person Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/36B3F450786FDD30DEED3E70ECBB75B9/jobs/476084": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Entrepreneurship, Ior in Entrepreneurship, Innovation and Leadership Development",
      "description": "You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Assistant Professor in Entrepreneurship, Ior in Entrepreneurship, Innovation and Leadership Development MIAMI GARDENS, FL 33054 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Apply St. Thomas University - Gus Machado College of Business Description: The Gus Machado College of Business at St. Thomas University invites applications for a full-time, 9-month/academic year, faculty position at the Assistant Professor level in the area of Entrepreneurship, Innovation and Leadership Development for Fall/Spring 2026-2027 . Candidates with a particular focus on: Entrepreneurship and New Venture Creation Management Consulting, and Leadership Development are encouraged to apply. Requirements: Candidates must have a doctoral degree from a regionally accredited institution at the time of hire in Business Administration, Entrepreneurship, New Venture Creation, Management Consulting, or Leadership Development or other related area with outstanding academic credentials that clearly demonstrate their ability to teach courses and conduct independent and successful research in Entrepreneurship, New Venture Creation, Management Consulting, and Leadership Development , and extensive professional experience in the field. Candidates must have excellent communication skills with a commitment to engage in a first-rate undergraduate and graduate education. Responsibilities for the positions include teaching, student advising and mentoring at both the undergraduate and graduate levels, and development of programs. The academic responsibilities at the Gus Machado College of Business at St. Thomas University include teaching undergraduate and graduate courses and research in the Entrepreneurship, Innovation, New Venture Creation, Management Consulting, and Leadership Development , and related areas and service. The teaching responsibilities include lecturing, hands-on lab exercises, and student mentoring. The successful candidate will have a passion for teaching, hands-on learning, supervising undergraduate and graduate research projects, and mentoring students. The desired candidate will have an established research and professional experience record in Entrepreneurship, New Venture Creation, Innovation, and Leadership Development or related areas and must be able to comingle and interact effectively with industry and government personnel in the Entrepreneurship, New Venture Creation, Innovation, Small Business Development, Leadership and Community Development domains. The MBA program at the Gus Machado College of Business at St. Thomas University is characterized by a multi-disciplinary approach to the curriculum. Student-learning incorporates significant lab and hands-on activities that translate theory into practice. St. Thomas University is a Catholic University accredited by the Commission of Colleges of the Southern Association of Colleges and Schools (SACS) to award baccalaureate, masters, law, and doctoral degrees and is a is a student-centered teaching institution dedicated to developing ethical leaders for life. Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: An earned doctorate in Business Administration or Leadership or in a related area with demonstrated experience in Entrepreneurship, New Venture Creation, Innovation, Incubator Operations, Management Consulting, or Leadership Development. Evidence of/potential for scholarly work. Evidence of professional experience in Entrepreneurship, New Venture Creation, Innovation, Incubator Operations, Management Consulting, or Leadership Development or related domains. Evidence of successful grant procurement related to Entrepreneurship, Small Business creation, Incubator Operations, Community or Leadership Development Experience collaborating with industry on research and working in incubator type operations. Experience in college-level teaching, mentoring, and research consistent with appointment to the rank of Assistant Professor. Application Procedures: Application packets should include: (a) current curriculum vita; (b) a statement of interest, including achievements and how the applicant will contribute to in areas of teaching, research, and service; and (c) names and contact information of three academic/professional references; (d) copies of post-secondary degree transcripts. Screening of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/36B3F450786FDD30DEED3E70ECBB75B9/jobs/476138": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Academic Success and Bar Preparation",
      "description": "You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Assistant Professor of Academic Success and Bar Preparation MIAMI GARDENS, FL 33054 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Apply St. Thomas University - College of Law Position Summary: The Assistant Professor of Academic Success and Bar Preparation reports directly to the Assistant Dean of Academic Success and Bar Preparation. This is a faculty position. This position is dedicated to enhancing the academic and professional success of law students and recent graduates through high-quality instruction, individualized support, and targeted programming in academic success and bar preparation. Primary Responsibilities: Participate in the design, development, implementation, and continuous improvement of academic success and bar preparation courses, workshops, and related programming. Teach academic success and bar preparation courses as assigned. Create and maintain student support resources, including Canvas pages, SharePoint sites, CALI Lessons, and other academic tools. Advise and mentor students on academic success strategies, course planning, bar readiness, and personal and professional development. Develop and deliver workshops and related programming on essential academic skills, bar exam strategies, and student success. Provide instruction and feedback on legal reasoning, writing, and study strategies. Maintain a professional, supportive rapport with students, faculty, and staff. Collaborate with faculty and administration to align academic success and bar preparation programming with evolving bar exam formats, including the NextGen Bar Exam. Ensure confidentiality and professionalism in all student interactions. Maintain accurate records of individual student meetings and progress. Support and uphold the mission, vision, and values of the law school. Perform additional academic support duties as assigned. Participate in the design and implementation of bar preparation courses Stay current on developments in bar exam formats, trends, and preparation strategies. Provide individualized bar preparation support, maintaining consistent weekly contact with assigned bar takers via email and/or messaging system. Maintain accurate and timely records of student meetings and progress. Administrative Duties Ensure compliance with law school and university policies, procedures, and accreditation standards. Adhere to all departmental and university safety and conduct regulations. This is a campus-based position requiring consistent on-campus presence during regular business hours. Qualifications Required Qualifications: Juris Doctor (J.D.) degree from an accredited law school. Licensed and in good standing with a state bar. Minimum of 2–3 years of legal experience, or a combination of education and experience demonstrating equivalent skills. Strong knowledge of academic success and bar exam strategies, with UBE bar exam experience and familiarity with the NextGen Bar Exam preferred. Demonstrated ability to build strong relationships with students, faculty, staff, and legal professionals. Proven initiative, sound judgment, and a collaborative approach to supporting student success. Ability to adapt to evolving institutional needs and responsibilities. Proficiency in Microsoft Office and other common digital platforms. Strong organizational skills, attention to detail, and professional demeanor. Ability to lift and carry up to 20 pounds on occasion, consistent with a typical office environment. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/36B3F450786FDD30DEED3E70ECBB75B9/jobs/476196": {
      "title": "Law Library Circulation Specialist (Part-Time)",
      "description": "You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Law Library Circulation Specialist (Part-Time) MIAMI GARDENS, FL 33054 Apply Overview Position Type Part Time Apply St. Thomas University - Law Library Summary Under the direction of the Law Library Circulation Manager, this staff member will be primarily responsible for Circulation Desk daily processes and activities such as providing customer service to all patrons, providing assistance to in locating library materials, stack maintenance, processing circulation transactions (check-in/check-out of all library materials including study rooms, monitoring circulation email requests, assisting the Circulation Manager in the supervision of the student assistants, and general collection maintenance. This position may be assigned to work closely with the Technical Services staff concerning stack maintenance, shelving of library materials and special projects. This position may oversee the opening and closing of the library. Essential Functions To be a productive member of the Law Library Team, and as an important member of the team, this staff member will perform whatever task or function required to meet the evolving needs of the College of Law community including students, faculty, and patrons. Team members will be readily available and visible to students, faculty, and patrons. Every effort will be made to answer patron inquiries. If unable to answer an inquiry, the team member will ensure that the customer is assisted by another member of the Law Library team or staff. Circulation Perform all opening/closing procedures as directed. Upon opening the library, ensure that the Circulation Desk as well as the library are ready for daily operation. Oversee the check-in/out of library materials of various formats. Forward damaged library materials upon check-in to the Technical Services Department for repair or replacement. Oversee the reservation and check-in/out of study rooms/study tables. Assist the Circulation Manager in organizing and directing overdue notices. Recommend changes and new policies and procedures that may need updating or changing to the Circulation Manager. Implement any changes as directed. Assist in keeping Circulation Department manuals up to date. Communicate these policies to library patrons. Assist and patrons in the use of WMS, the library online public access catalog. Assist students with printing/photocopy needs, ensure that printers/copiers are stocked with paper and are functioning properly. Communicate with OIT (Office of Information Technology) to report malfunctions or problems with network access. Ensure sure that all study rooms are available and ready for use. Ensure that all office supplies areas (staplers, hole puncher, etc.) are stocked and functional. Inform the Circulation Manager of any supply needs for the department. Refer any reference questions to a librarian. 2 Collection Maintenance Shelving, shelf reading and shifting of the library collection as needed. This entails working closely with the staff in the Technical Services department. Recommend the replacement or discard of damaged and obsolete library materials to the Technical Services Department Other duties Perform any duties assigned by Circulation Manager or librarians. Assist in collecting data related to collection use, circulation desk transactions and building use. May be required to represent the Law Library in Iocal library meetings as requested. Report to the Circulation Manager any library building issues that require maintenance. Work in other areas and perform other tasks as assigned. Qualifications Competencies Ability to communicate effectively and courteously. Ability to work as a team player and deal cooperatively with others. Ability to interpret a variety of instructions in either written, oral or schedule form. Ability to understand library system technology in order to assist patrons successfully. Ability to acquire a working knowledge of regulations and procedures pertaining to library responsibilities. Strong and effective communication skills. Strong service orientation. Ability to multitask. Be flexible with work assignments and work hours as needed. Supervisory Responsibility This position does not have supervisory responsibility, it may assist the Circulation Manager in the direction and training of the law library assistants assigned to the Circulation Department. Work Environment/Physical Demands The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. While performing the duties of this job, the employee is occasionally required to stand, walk; sit; reach with hands and arms; climb stairs; push library carts full of books; climb on stands to shelf books. The employee must occasionally lift of move library materials and supplies, up to 30 pounds. Position Type/Expected Hours of Work This is a Part-time position. Days and hours of work may require daytime, evening, weekend and holiday hours. Travel This position does not require any travel. Education and Experience Bachelor’s degree is required. Library experience is preferred. Other Duties Please note this job description is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time with or without notice. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/36B3F450786FDD30DEED3E70ECBB75B9/jobs/476180": {
      "title": "Online Assistant Professor of Nursing - Psychiatric Mental Health Nurse Practitioner (PMHNP)",
      "description": "You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Online Assistant Professor of Nursing - Psychiatric Mental Health Nurse Practitioner (PMHNP) MIAMI GARDENS, FL 33054 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Apply St. Thomas University - Nursing Position Overview: St. Thomas University College of Nursing invites applications for an online full-time Assistant/Associate Professor of Nursing position in the Psychiatric Mental Health Nursing Practitioner Program. The successful candidate will play a key role in shaping the future of the various nursing programs through teaching, clinical supervision, research, and service. This faculty member will contribute to the development of nursing students at the graduate level, delivering a student-centered educational experience in line with the University’s mission of fostering ethical leadership, cultural diversity and academic excellence that reflect our Catholic identity. The position offers opportunities for professional growth, collaboration, and making a significant impact in nursing education. Key Responsibilities: Teach graduate nursing courses, including general and specialized ones in your area of expertise, such as Psychiatric Mental Health Nurse Practitioner (PMHNP). Develop and implement innovative, evidence-based teaching strategies for online learning environments. Provide academic advising and mentorship to students, helping them set academic and professional goals. Engage in curriculum development, program assessment and evaluation, and continuous improvement initiatives for nursing programs. Participate in faculty meetings and accreditation-related activities, including assisting the Dean of Nursing with the preparation of accreditation documents. Maintain office hours as per St. Thomas University guidelines and support the program’s goals through direct involvement in faculty initiatives. Actively participate in simulation-based learning activities as needed. Collaborate with faculty members to enhance student learning, clinical placements, and program development. Participate in departmental, college, and university service activities, including faculty committees and community engagement. Foster a collaborative, inclusive, and supportive learning environment that promotes student success and addresses the needs of a diverse student population. Conduct and publish research in areas related to nursing practice, education, or healthcare. Stay current with advances in nursing practice and education to continuously improve teaching and clinical instruction. Qualifications Required Qualifications: Education Background: Ph.D. or DNP (Doctor of Nursing Practice) in Nursing from an accredited institution. Master of Science in Nursing (MSN) with a Psychiatric Mental Health Nurse Practitioner. Certification: National certification as a Psychiatric Mental Health Nurse Practitioner (PMHNP). Licensure: Unencumbered Registered Nurse (RN) and APRN license in the State of Florida. Experience: Application Instructions: Please submit the following along with your application Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Contact Information for Three Professional References Statement of Teaching Philosophy Copies of Post-Secondary Degree Transcripts Florida Nursing License St. Thomas University is an E-Verify Equal Opportunity Employer. Criminal background checks are conducted as part of the employment process. Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/36B3F450786FDD30DEED3E70ECBB75B9/jobs/477323": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant, Bobcat Academic Achievement Center (BAAC)",
      "description": "You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Administrative Assistant, Bobcat Academic Achievement Center (BAAC) MIAMI GARDENS, FL 33054 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Apply St. Thomas University - Bobcat Academic Achievement Center Position Summary: The Administrative Assistant provides comprehensive administrative and operational support for university-wide academic advising in The Bobcat Academic Achievement Center. Serving as the primary point of contact for students, faculty, staff, and visitors, this position ensures efficient office operations while delivering exceptional customer service. The Administrative Assistant manages front office functions, coordinates student appointments and schedules, maintains confidential records, supports advising initiatives, and assists with special projects and events that contribute to student success and retention. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: Student Services Serve as the first point of contact for students, parents, faculty, and campus partners by providing accurate information and directing inquiries appropriately. Welcome students and visitors in a professional, inclusive, and customer-focused manner. Schedule advising appointments. Assist students with navigating advising resources, forms, and university processes. Monitor advising center communications, including email, telephone, and online inquiries, ensuring timely responses and appropriate follow-up. Maintain confidentiality of student information in accordance with FERPA and university policies. Administrative Support Provide administrative support to the Center’s staff. Manage calendars, meeting schedules, conference room reservations, and departmental events. Prepare correspondence, reports, presentations, agendas, and meeting minutes. Process purchase requests, invoices, travel arrangements, and other administrative transactions in accordance with university procedures. Order and maintain office supplies and coordinate equipment maintenance. Assist in planning and coordinating programs, registration events, advising workshops, and student success initiatives. Prepare event materials, signage, communications, and participant resources. Other duties as assigned. Qualifications Minimum Qualifications Associate's degree in business administration, office administration, or a related field; bachelor's degree preferred. Two years of responsible administrative support or customer service experience, preferably in higher education. Demonstrated proficiency with Microsoft Office Suite (Word, Excel, Outlook, PowerPoint) and standard office technology. Experience scheduling appointments and maintaining calendars. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Strong organizational skills with the ability to prioritize multiple responsibilities in a fast-paced environment. Demonstrated attention to detail and accuracy. Ability to exercise sound judgment and maintain confidentiality. Commitment to providing outstanding customer service and working effectively with individuals from diverse backgrounds. Preferred Qualifications Experience working in higher education, academic advising, or student services. Knowledge of FERPA regulations and university administrative processes. Strong interpersonal and relationship-building skills. Ability to communicate effectively with students, faculty, staff, and external constituents. Strong technology skills and the ability to learn new software applications. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/36B3F450786FDD30DEED3E70ECBB75B9/jobs/477484": {
      "title": "Executive Coordinator",
      "description": "You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Executive Coordinator MIAMI GARDENS, FL 33054 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Apply St. Thomas University - Human Rights Initiative POSITION SUMMARY : The Executive Coordinator provides recruitment, strategic and administrative leadership for the LL.M./J.S.D. Program in Intercultural Human Rights (ICHRP). Reporting to the Program Director, the Executive Coordinator leads student recruitment, program promotion, and enrollment initiatives to advance the Program’s outreach, partnerships, and public impact and engagement efforts. The Executive Coordinator also supports budgeting and project administration. This role also supports executive-level functions such as strategic planning, event creation and oversight, communications, grant development, and media relations while serving as the primary point of contact for prospective students, faculty, government agencies, NGOs, and international partners. ABOUT ST. THOMAS UNIVERSITY COLLEGE OF LAW: Founded in 1984, College of Law is one of the most diverse access law schools in the United States. It is part of St. Thomas University, founded in 1961 as Biscayne College by the order of the Augustinian Friars. St. Thomas University is an urban, student-centered, Catholic university with rich cultural and international diversity, dedicated to developing leaders who contribute to the economic and cultural vitality of the regions they serve. To this end, the College of Law remains committed in teaching, scholarship, and service, to fostering a public order of human dignity, to training lawyers sensitive to the needs of the region’s underrepresented communities, and to expanding access to professional opportunities which includes active partnerships with business, government, and the South Florida Community. Equal Opportunity: St. Thomas University provides equality of opportunity in education for all persons, including faculty and staff (with respect to recruitment, hiring, retention, promotion, tenure, compensation, terms and conditions of employment, termination, and the like) and students, including applicants for admission and enrolled students (with respect to admission, retention, and the like), except that the University (1) will maintain its Catholic values in the operation of the University, and (2) may exercise a preference for Catholic faculty in recruitment and hiring. (The general norm of the Apostolic Constitution on Catholic Universities states that “the number of non-Catholic teachers should not be allowed to constitute a majority within the institution.”) St. Thomas University also provides its students and graduates with equal opportunity to obtain employment, including the requirement that every employer to whom it furnishes assistance and facilities for interviewing and other placement services must observe the principles of equal opportunity. Nondiscrimination: Except for the maintenance of Catholic values in the operation of the University and a preference for Catholic faculty in recruitment and hiring, discrimination on the basis of race, color, ethnicity, religion, national origin, sex, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, age, disability, or military status, marital or familial status, or any other category that is or becomes protected by law, is strictly prohibited. Accreditation: St. Thomas University College of Law is fully accredited by the American Bar Association and is a member of the Association of American Law Schools (AALS). St. Thomas University is accredited by the Southern Association of Colleges and Schools Commission on Colleges ROLES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Principal responsibility: recruitment and enrollment of LL.M. and J.S.D. students in Intercultural Human Rights. Research, consult, plan, and design constituent components (including budgeting) of a good promotional strategy for the Master’s and Doctoral programs. Establish the procedure to advertise the programs and identify the respective fora of advertisement, including drafting the substance of the advertising tool/ modality, selecting appropriate and effective visual material, suggest, approve the design of ads, review, and approve the various fora of advertising etc. Develop enrollment marketing publications and communications including fliers, brochures, viewbooks, website postings, electronic mail and other media, including an effective social media presence. Identify, network with recruiting agencies, and participate in recruiting events. Devise and implement strategic planning initiatives regarding on/off campus recruiting events, and perform outreach to colleges and universities, organizations, and prospective students. Develop and manage a robust recruiting calendar. Plan, coordinate, and execute program informational sessions throughout the year, open houses, and admitted Students events). Admissions -- collect and review for accuracy all application materials from prospective students: application form, resume, personal statement, letters of recommendation, transcripts, credential evaluations, writing samples etc. Coordinate and help conduct in person or Zoom interviews of the applicant with the Director. Implement admissions communications and applicant engagement strategies, and provide information on distinguished faculty, costs of the program and funding resources available, including scholarships. Pay particular attention to foreign credentials, respective evaluations, translations, and the requirements for foreign student visas etc. Offer recommendations to the Director for decisions (accept/ reject/ waitlist). Assist with planning, coordination, and execution of Orientation Events. Implement program activities, including research projects, conferences, training programs, and special events. Draft budget and explore additional resources for the program as well as for extra- or co-curricular activities, or community related activities. Coordinate with the Director to develop and implement academic enhancement programs for students. Perform other related duties as required by the Director. Qualifications POSITION QUALIFICATIONS/SPECIFICATIONS: Bachelor’s degree required; advanced degree in international relations, human rights or related field preferred. Preferably, at least 3 years of experience in graduate student recruitment. Knowledge and experience of project and budget management. Strong written and verbal communication skills; fluency in English required (Spanish preferred). Ability to build partnerships and work effectively in diverse multicultural environments. Ability to work flexible hours, travel locally, and manage multiple priorities under deadlines. Proven managerial, day-to-day problem-solving, negotiation and interpersonal skills. Proficiency in standard computer programs and digital communications tools. High level of discretion, professionalism, and integrity. Physical requirements are within the normal bounds of an office environment but may include occasional lifting, carrying, pushing/pulling up to 20 pounds. SUPERVISION RECEIVED: Executive Coordinator reports to the Director of the LL.M./J.S.D. in Intercultural Human Rights Program. SUPERVISION EXERCISED : Graduate Fellows and/or Research Assistants (as needed) Consultants (as neded) Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/36B3F450786FDD30DEED3E70ECBB75B9/jobs/477474": {
      "title": "Major Gift Officer",
      "description": "You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Major Gift Officer MIAMI GARDENS, FL 33054 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Apply St. Thomas University - Philanthropy Position Overview The Major Gift Officer, is responsible for identifying, cultivating, soliciting, and stewarding a portfolio of major gift prospects in support of St. Thomas University’s fundraising priorities. This position manages a portfolio of individuals, families, foundations, and other constituents capable of making gifts at the major gift level, and is accountable for achieving defined annual fundraising goals. The Major Gifts Officer builds and maintains long-term relationships with donors through strategic engagement, personalized communication, and face-to-face visits, to secure significant outright, multi-year, and planned gifts. Working as part of the overall Philanthropy team in the Office of Philanthropy, this position plays a key role in advancing the university’s comprehensive campaign priorities, endowments, scholarships, academic programs, athletics, and capital initiatives. The Major Gifts Officer, collaborates closely with the Vice President of Philanthropy, Deans, faculty, and volunteer leadership in the identification, cultivation, and solicitation of prospects, and provides regular reporting, strategy development, and stewardship to ensure continued donor engagement and growth in philanthropic investment. Key Responsibilities include, but are not limited to: Manages an assigned portfolio of major gift prospects and donors, developing and executing individualized cultivation, solicitation, and stewardship strategies. Conducts face-to-face visits and virtual meetings to qualify, cultivate, solicit, and steward donors, with a focus on securing gifts at the major gift level and above. Develops and presents written proposals, gift agreements, and funding priorities aligned with donor interests and institutional needs. Collaborates with the Vice President of Philanthropy solicitation strategies and donor engagement opportunities. Identifies and qualifies new major gift prospects through referrals, research, annual fund upgrades, and discovery visits. Ensures accurate and timely documentation of donor interactions, strategies, proposals, and moves management activity in Raiser’s Edge/NXT. Provides ongoing stewardship to donors, including impact reporting, recognition, and meaningful engagement opportunities. Participates in campaign planning, leadership gift strategies, and special initiatives, including endowments, capital projects, and named giving opportunities. Works closely with Annual Fund, Alumni Engagement, Events, and Advancement Operations to support pipeline development and donor progression. Assists in the development of major gift fundraising goals, forecasts, and performance reports. Seeks appropriate training opportunities to maintain and enhance professional fundraising skills, particularly in major gift solicitation, donor strategy, and relationship management. Performs other duties as assigned. Qualifications Required Skills & Competencies Strong relationship-building and interpersonal skills Strategic and results-oriented mindset Ability to manage multiple prospects and priorities simultaneously Excellent verbal and written communication skills Demonstrated ability to conduct effective donor visits and solicitations Proficiency with CRM systems (Raiser’s Edge/NXT preferred) and Microsoft Office Professional, collaborative, and donor-centered approach Ability to create meaningful donor experiences, build trust, and advance long-term philanthropic partnerships Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/36B3F450786FDD30DEED3E70ECBB75B9/jobs/477305": {
      "title": "Office Assistant, Counseling Center & Student Health Services",
      "description": "You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Office Assistant, Counseling Center & Student Health Services MIAMI GARDENS, FL 33054 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Apply St. Thomas University - Student Affairs POSITION SUMMARY : Reporting to the Student Health Services & Counseling Center, the Office Assistant provides daily administrative and clerical support to the Center, schedules appointments, oversees the student health insurance program, vaccinations and immunization records, and assists the health services and counseling center staff by scheduling appointments and maintain student records. CHARACTERISTIC DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES: Serves as the office receptionist by greeting students and ensuring they are served in a professional manner and within a reasonable time. Schedules appointments and assists the Director and Personal Counselor with receiving, screening, and returning telephone calls as appropriate. Coordinates the student health insurance program in cooperation with the STU Business Office to ensure students are providing accurate insurance information or enrolling in the STU student health insurance program. Collecting, reviewing, and processing Student Immunization Records. Maintains confidential student files including maintaining accurate records of student health insurance information. Prepares, assembles, and distributes materials for mailings and correspondence related to the department. Orders and maintains office supplies and processes related invoices and expenses. Manages the department's website pages and provides updates as needed. Performs other duties for the department and division as assigned. S UPERVISION EXERCISED: Supervise student employees. Qualifications POSITION QUALIFICATIONS/SPECIFICATIONS: High school diploma/degree required; associate or bachelor's degree preferred. 1-3 years office, administrative, secretary, or receptionist experience required, preferably in a health service, medical office, or higher education setting. Knowledge and use of computers including Microsoft Office packages and Outlook. A willingness to develop computer skills and adjust to current technology as required. Strong communication and interpersonal skills; student and family focused. Understanding and commitment to maintain privacy and confidentiality. Professionalism and strong customer relations skills needed to interact with students, families, staff, and faculty. Ability to work independently and follow through with tasks and responsibilities with an attention to detail. Ability to maintain confidential information with the utmost discretion and sensitivity (Title IX, FERPA, HIPAA). Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/36B3F450786FDD30DEED3E70ECBB75B9/jobs/449391": {
      "title": "Public Safety Officer II",
      "description": "You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Public Safety Officer II MIAMI GARDENS, FL 33054 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Apply St. Thomas University - Public Safety POSITION SUMMARY: The non-exempt hourly position is a specialized public safety officer II (PSO) responsible for maintaining safety, security, and order within the University campus, residence halls, and surrounding footprint. They serve as a visible presence, support student wellbeing, and coordinate closely with university stakeholders including Office of Student Affairs and Student Life, Office of Residential Living, faculty, and staff. This is a 24-hour operation which requires the ability to work an atypical schedule to meet operational necessity, with varied shifts, including weekends and holidays. This position is classified as essential personnel and may require reporting to duty during emergencies or natural disasters, and special events. Adherence to established public safety uniform and grooming standards is mandatory. The PSO II may be called upon to be shift lead and may p erform collateral duties as a Field Training Officer for newly hired officers to mentor, coach, and train them in duties of the job. The PSO II may serve as the Acting Shift Supervisor in their absence. ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES: Patrol campus on golf cart, vehicle or on foot, inclusive of Residential Halls Respond to noise complaints or disturbances Monitor CCTV or alarm systems Escort students, faculty and staff upon request Conduct Safety checks (doors, lighting, emergency equipment) in collaboration with Resident Assistance Incident documentation and communication with dispatch Detect and respond to safety hazards to ensure safety of students, faculty, staff and visitors. Provide physical inspections and investigation on campus to ensure a safe environment. Conduct security and safety audits to ensure that hazards and dangers are identified. Conduct Residential Room checks in collaboration with the Office of Residential Life. Maintain certifications as appropriate, to include CPR, AED, tourniquet, crowd manager, etc. Conducts accident and injury investigations on campus to ensure proper record keeping of incidents. Complete activity logs, inspection reports and incident reports to ensure proper record keeping of incidents. Coordinate with local University Leadership, Clery Administrators, local law enforcement concerning the investigation of incidents, crimes, and losses. Attend collaboration meetings with Office of Residential Life, Resident Assistants, and other University stakeholders. Conduct fire systems, life safety inspections and emergency response drills. Lock and unlock access control for campus buildings. Perform other duties as assigned or required. Qualifications MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS TO QUALIFY FOR PSO II: Associate’s degree or at least sixty (60) college credits; OR High school diploma or equivalent with (2) years of active or reserve military duty; OR prior State or Federal Certified Law Enforcement Officer; OR Certified State of Florida Guardian with a minimum of 1 year of employment in that role; OR four years of continuous, post-high school work in a Higher Education setting. Valid driver's license. Investigative Experience Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    }
  },
  "rows": {
